  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the National Program on the Response to HIV Epicemic in the Republic of Armenia (Program) - Armenia (01-Oct-2012-31-Dec-2015)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While Armenia is still a country with a concentrated HIV epidemic, it has seen a substantial growth of identified HIV cases over the past six years, partially due to increased voluntary counseling and testing services. This program implemented by Mission East aims to improve access to counseling and testing among most-at-risk populations, HIV prevention activities among injecting drug users, sex workers, men who have sex with men, most-at-risk adolescents aged 15-17; peer education among youth (15-24 years old); care and support to adults and children living with and affected by HIV; and institutional capacity building of civil society organizations.</narrative>
  </description>
